{
  "comment": "The declared harnesses of `tools/check-case-names.sh`: one row per suite that runs cases, and the names each row declares are the only names a shipped spec's `**Case**:` line may resolve to. `kind` is how the names are read: `file` greps `pattern` (with `prefix`) out of `path`, `command` runs `command` and reads the names it prints, and `classes` reads one case per test method from `roots` (`.path`, `.module`, optional `.qualifier` such as `device`). `groups` is the set of case-group prefixes the row claims — a group two rows claim is a DECLARED fact and is printed once, never refused; an identical full name in two rows IS refused. `exclude` is a delegation: the row prints the names but another row's bodies run them, and the check refuses an exclusion that hides a name no other row declares. The four shipped rows the change names are `loop`, `sensors`, `issues-core` and `gradle`; the rest are the suites a shipped spec already cites, and a suite added to the tree with no row here is a name that resolves to nothing — the check names it rather than trusting it.",
  "harnesses": [
    {
      "id": "loop",
      "kind": "command",
      "command": ["bash", "tools/loop/tests/loop-selftest.sh", "--list"],
      "groups": ["adapter", "census", "check", "clean", "core", "driver", "evidence", "gate", "labels", "look", "measure", "mutation", "phase", "policy", "prescreen", "prompt", "repeat", "report", "run", "state", "trim", "usage", "worktree"],
      "why": "`tools/loop/**` is the loop's own suite, the largest case set in the tree; `--list` prints its array, so a case added to the suite is declared on the same commit that adds it. `check` and `core` are shared claims, not renames: `check#aRouteSectionResolvesAgainstItsDocument` asserts the loop's own evidence-check route (the `check` group `check-metadata` and `issues-core` also name), and `core#*` asserts `tools/loop/core/` (the `core` group the `gradle` row also names as a module)."
    },
    {
      "id": "sensors",
      "kind": "command",
      "command": ["bash", "tools/sensors/tests/sensor-selftest.sh", "--list"],
      "groups": ["Registry", "close", "create", "guard", "hotspot", "layers", "lib", "reopen", "report", "run", "sensors", "update", "workflow"],
      "why": "the sensor tooling's shell cases; `run` is shared with the loop row on purpose — two lifecycle suites both name a group `run`, and the shared claim is declared here rather than renamed."
    },
    {
      "id": "issues-core",
      "kind": "command",
      "command": ["bash", "tools/issues/tests/issue-tooling-selftest.sh", "--list"],
      "groups": ["Bands", "Fingerprint", "Policy", "Profile", "Taxonomy", "TodoSections", "WorkPackage", "adapter", "answer", "basis", "check", "classify", "close", "create", "decision-queue", "decisions", "docs", "duplicates", "import", "labels", "lib", "list", "metadata", "policy", "prioritise", "queue", "shaping", "surface", "update"],
      "exclude": "^check#",
      "why": "the issue tooling's Java cases (`tools/issues/core/Cases.java`) plus its shell cases; the `check#*` names are printed here because the shell runner delegates them to `check-metadata`, whose row owns the bodies, so they are excluded from this row and a `hinges` refusal fires if the metadata row ever stops declaring one."
    },
    {
      "id": "check-metadata",
      "kind": "command",
      "command": ["bash", "tools/issues/tests/check-metadata-selftest.sh", "--list"],
      "groups": ["check"],
      "why": "the metadata checker's falsification: it owns the `check#*` bodies the issue tooling's runner delegates to."
    },
    {
      "id": "resolve-stale",
      "kind": "command",
      "command": ["bash", "tools/issues/tests/resolve-stale-selftest.sh", "--list"],
      "groups": ["classifier", "pipeline", "prescreen", "resolver"],
      "why": "the stale-citation repair, whose cases the issue tooling's runner also names; that row excludes them."
    },
    {
      "id": "gradle",
      "kind": "classes",
      "roots": [
        {"path": "app/src/test", "module": "app"},
        {"path": "app/src/androidTest", "module": "app", "qualifier": "device"},
        {"path": "auto/src/test", "module": "auto"},
        {"path": "core/src/test", "module": "core"},
        {"path": "buildSrc/src/test", "module": "buildSrc"},
        {"path": "architecture/src/test", "module": "architecture"},
        {"path": "osmscout-client-java/src/test", "module": "osmscout-client-java"}
      ],
      "groups": ["app", "app(device)", "auto", "core", "buildSrc", "architecture", "osmscout-client-java"],
      "why": "the Gradle test trees: a case is one test method, `Class.method` or `Class#method`, and a test class with no method is itself a case; a bare `Class` form is declared only where no second module of this row holds the same class name, so a bare reference to a class two modules hold is refused instead of guessed."
    },
    {
      "id": "native",
      "kind": "classes",
      "roots": [
        {"path": "app/src/main/cpp/libosmscout/Tests/src", "module": "libosmscout"}
      ],
      "groups": ["libosmscout"],
      "bare": false,
      "why": "the submodule's Catch2 suite: `TEST_CASE` carries a sentence, not an identifier, so a case is its translation unit's class — `libosmscout: RouteStepModelTest` — and no method form is declared because the suite names none."
    },
    {
